---
/** the loop: a hypernetwork predicts a weight edit from a task description, test-time learning refines it, and the error after refinement trains the hypernetwork only. */
const B = { w: 198, h: 66 };
const L = 12, R = 250, T = 96, D = 236;
const WB = { x: R + 24, y: 14, w: 150, h: 44 }; // the frozen foundation model
---
<figure class="fig fig-loop">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 460 350" role="img" aria-label="a loop of four steps. a hypernetwork with parameters phi reads the task description and predicts an edit delta W. the edit is added to the frozen foundation model W. one or two steps of self-supervised test-time learning refine the edited weights. the prediction error after that is backpropagated through the test-time steps into phi: only the hypernetwork is updated, W stays frozen.">
    <defs>
      <marker id="loop-arrow" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" class="arrowhead" /></marker>
      <marker id="loop-arrow-hot" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 z" class="arrowhead hot" /></marker>
    </defs>

    <text x={L} y="30" class="fig-t">task description</text>
    <line x1={L + 50} y1="38" x2={L + 50} y2={T - 2} class="wire" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />

    <rect x={WB.x} y={WB.y} width={WB.w} height={WB.h} class="frame limit" />
    <text x={WB.x + 10} y={WB.y + 18} class="fig-t">foundation model W</text>
    <text x={WB.x + 10} y={WB.y + 34} class="fig-t dim">frozen</text>
    <line x1={WB.x + WB.w / 2} y1={WB.y + WB.h} x2={WB.x + WB.w / 2} y2={T - 2} class="wire" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />
    <text x={WB.x + WB.w / 2 + 8} y={(WB.y + WB.h + T) / 2 + 4} class="fig-t dim">+</text>

    <rect x={L} y={T} width={B.w} height={B.h} class="node trained" />
    <text x={L + 12} y={T + 22} class="fig-h">1  hypernetwork H<tspan dy="3" font-size="10">φ</tspan></text>
    <text x={L + 12} y={T + 42} class="fig-t">reads the task,</text>
    <text x={L + 12} y={T + 58} class="fig-t">predicts the edit</text>

    <line x1={L + B.w} y1={T + B.h / 2} x2={R - 2} y2={T + B.h / 2} class="wire" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />
    <text x={L + B.w + 4} y={T + B.h / 2 - 7} class="fig-t">ΔW</text>

    <rect x={R} y={T} width={B.w} height={B.h} class="node" />
    <text x={R + 12} y={T + 22} class="fig-h">2  edited model</text>
    <text x={R + 12} y={T + 42} class="fig-t">W + ΔW</text>
    <text x={R + 12} y={T + 58} class="fig-t dim">ΔW is low-rank</text>

    <line x1={R + B.w / 2} y1={T + B.h} x2={R + B.w / 2} y2={D - 2} class="wire" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />

    <rect x={R} y={D} width={B.w} height={B.h} class="node" />
    <text x={R + 12} y={D + 22} class="fig-h">3  test-time learning</text>
    <text x={R + 12} y={D + 42} class="fig-t">1–2 self-supervised steps</text>
    <text x={R + 12} y={D + 58} class="fig-t dim">W + ΔW  →  W + ΔW′</text>

    <line x1={R} y1={D + B.h / 2} x2={L + B.w + 2} y2={D + B.h / 2} class="wire" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow)" />

    <rect x={L} y={D} width={B.w} height={B.h} class="node" />
    <text x={L + 12} y={D + 22} class="fig-h">4  prediction error</text>
    <text x={L + 12} y={D + 42} class="fig-t">of W + ΔW′ on the task</text>

    <line x1={L + 50} y1={D} x2={L + 50} y2={T + B.h + 2} class="wire update" marker-end="url(#loop-arrow-hot)" />
    <text x={L + 60} y={(T + B.h + D) / 2 - 4} class="fig-t hot-t">backprop through step 3</text>
    <text x={L + 60} y={(T + B.h + D) / 2 + 11} class="fig-t hot-t">updates φ only</text>

    <text x={L} y="340" class="fig-t dim">W never changes. ΔW′ is thrown away after the task.</text>
  </svg>
  <p class="fig-legend" aria-hidden="true"><span><i class="sw trained"></i>the only thing that gets trained</span><span><i class="sw frozen"></i>frozen</span></p>
  <figcaption>the hypernetwork learns to propose a starting point that a few steps of test-time learning can take far, not the final weights.</figcaption>
</figure>
